<Project>
  <!--
    Intentionally does NOT chain to the repo-root Directory.Build.props.

    XamlTimeline is a standalone netstandard2.0 helper library shared by the WinUI
    viewer (multi-platform: x86/x64/ARM64) and the WPA plugin (AnyCPU). The repo-root
    build infrastructure (eng\configuration.props) redirects every project's obj /
    project.assets.json into a build-flavor-specific folder (amd64chk, x86fre, ...)
    derived from MUXOutputPlatform + MUXOutputConfiguration.

    When the multi-platform viewer references this AnyCPU library, MSBuild forwards
    the viewer's Platform (e.g. x64 => "amd64chk") down to XamlTimeline, but a clean
    restore only produced XamlTimeline's "chk"/"fre" flavors — so Visual Studio's
    design-time restore for Debug|x64 could not locate XamlTimeline's project
    information ("Unable to find project information for XamlTimeline.csproj").

    Keeping this project on vanilla SDK defaults gives it a single, stable,
    platform-agnostic obj\project.assets.json that every consumer (Visual Studio,
    the dotnet CLI, and the .ptix publish) can always find.
  -->
</Project>
